                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7cdefb1c-21ff-3615-acaa-5f1b0c3cc326",
                        "entry_id": "708b526c-aa1a-3004-a6ee-ccebece22143",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the voodoo religion, a spirit intermediary between Bondye (the creator god) and human beings."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a5960ab-0b5d-4d60-9732-dd1aa9e08415",
                                "sense_id": "7cdefb1c-21ff-3615-acaa-5f1b0c3cc326",
                                "text": "Here, on the Island Below the Sea, the loa have their permanent residence, their primal location."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "865330c0-f4af-4c64-a227-0069ebf64722",
                                "sense_id": "7cdefb1c-21ff-3615-acaa-5f1b0c3cc326",
                                "text": "Some will caution you at great length about the dangers of Vodou. They will tell you that the lwa are jealous, thin-skinned, and hot-tempered."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4fe639b0-4c95-461a-80bf-a84db44b3ec5",
                                "sense_id": "7cdefb1c-21ff-3615-acaa-5f1b0c3cc326",
                                "text": "Equally surprising is to find St Patrick so prominent in many Vodou shrines, until one remembers that he too had been a slave who had twice crossed the sea, the second time to freedom, and that he had particular power over snakes, like the loa (Haitian equivalent of orisha) Dambala Wèdo."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
